# The build needs the manifests, the app, the static files, the three configs
# vite reads, and the Caddyfile the final stage serves through. An allowlist
# rather than a list of things to keep out: .gitignore has no effect on a build
# context, and a denylist ships .env the day it is written under a name nobody
# thought to exclude.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!react-router.config.ts
!vite.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!app
!public
!Caddyfile
